{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/722530-anakim-s-birthright-in-a-full-crossover-game","id":722530,"title":"Anakim's Birthright in a full crossover game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-24T04:05:43-07:00","id":722530,"title":"Anakim's Birthright in a full crossover game.","content":"Just a couple of questions, personal shields e other forms of armor, can they count as physical obstacles? And living beings, can they count too? Can a beast destroy a magical shield of a mage or an effect that's acting as a obstacle to her desires?<br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T05:08:22-07:00","id":722608,"title":"","content":"That's a question you have to ask your ST. There's no definition of &quot;physical obsticle&quot; in the game, so its up to debate. Walls, a door on a safe, floors, etc all clearly count. Shields and armor are debatable, since its arguably thematic for a giant to tear armor off, but combat isn't an area it feels like the Birthright is meant to operate in. Living beings don't count - a power that can kill with absolutely no roll or save is clearly not inteded to replace combat, even if we talk about a mook. I think its clear that magical effects aren't physical, especially with the line about needing to spend Satiety to affect physical objects merely enhanced by magic, so a magical force field is beyond the Anakim's ability. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:01:31-07:00","id":723634,"title":"","content":"Other birthright also work in combat. I was thinking more in lines of generating some kind of tilt, like knockdown or something like that, nothing in the realms of insta-kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T06:27:10-07:00","id":728652,"title":"","content":"Other Birthrights specifically work by calling out specific combat Tilts and maneuvers. At no point does the Giant's Brightright say anything about destroying armor worn on someone or dealing damage to a person's health. The tone and wording of the abilities are completely different, which suggests to me that the intent isn't to have an all purpose combat ability. Plus, does having an innate Birthright that can instantly &quot;destroy&quot; an elder vamp, alpha wolf, archmage, or apex beast automatically make sense if they're standing in the way, as opposed to slightly to the side? No, it doesn't. <br /> <br /> As for generating Tilts? If the Birthright was meant to generate combat tilts, then it would have said them. It sounds too much like you're trying to get both the usual &quot;break through wall&quot; power on top of having a better Birthright than the Eshmaki, who need to be stealthed before they deal Tilts. Clearly, your suggestion is more powerful than the &quot;combat Birthrights&quot; so I'm exceedingly doubtful that's the intent of the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T12:26:51-07:00","id":729631,"title":"","content":"I would only say armor or shields count if they actually impede the anakim's path. Like a bunch of cops in riot gear creating a shield wall could have the anakim rip through the shield wall and I would argue that it would be fair if one or two of the riot shields end up broken. You can't use it to rip through a Kevlar vest someone is wearing. I would generally discount body armor as an acceptable target for the birthright.<br /> <br /> I might give a dice bonus if the objective is to plow through someone blocking a doorway. Though I would only allow it for forcing something out of the way, so it couldn't be used to destroy a bouncer who won't get out of the club doorway.<br /> <br /> A mage's barrier would be depending on the way the spell is functioning. For example a mage who's decided use his powers to replicate the DnD mage armor spell wouldn't be at risk of having the spell torn off by an anakim as the spell is basically making body-armor out of force. Whereas a mage standing in the middle of a circle of protection to prevent things from getting into the area would be vulnerable to having the barrier destroyed.(Would cost satiety though what with being magic and all.)<br /> <br /> Obstacles would need to present an actual physical obstacle to the desires to be a target. Locks, safes, walls, floors, bars, barriers, etc are fine. It wouldn't let one destroy a law that's obstructing them from doing something, a mental trauma wouldn't be a viable target for the birthright either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}